# libs: Import FFmpeg 9.0.2.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/12150 state=opened
# It introduces some build-time generated code, which we could generate by hand and commit the generated files, as they are relatively small, but I think it'd be nicer for makedep to be able to run some custom rules like implemented here. (That would be also useful if we ever want to integrate Mesa, as in https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/10531)

This also keeps arm64ec yuv2rgb with its previous implementation, and forks libswscale/aarch64/swscale_unscaled.c into the arm64ec subfolder, as I was unable to port the new aarch64 implementation. It seems to be using even more registers and I don't know arm64ec enough to be confident with the changes I make. The generated code (ops_asmgen.c, generating ops_lookup.gen.c and ops_neon.gen.S) also seems incompatible and would need to be reimplemented with less registers.
